! Compressible neo-Hookean elasticity with the stress postprocessing, which is a
! combination the suite did not have.
!
! Every neo-Hookean test that asks for stresses -- ContactPatch2DIncompressible,
! CooksMembrane3D, SD_CooksMembrane3D -- also sets "Mixed Formulation = True", so
! the pressure in the postprocessor always came from the solution as an unknown of
! the system. The compressible alternative, in which the pressure is the material's
! own volumetric response to the dilatation
!
!   p = lambda/2 (J - 1)(J + 1)
!
! was evaluated by nothing in the suite. The two 2-D neo-Hookean tests
! (NeoHookean2D, CooksMembrane) do exercise the compressible assembly, but neither
! asks for stresses, so they never reach this branch. Poisson ratio is 0.3 here,
! well away from the incompressible limit, so the compressible branch is the point
! of the test rather than an accident of it.
!
! WHAT THIS TEST IS AND IS NOT. There is no second solver to check against --
! StressSolve has no neo-Hookean model -- so unlike ElasticAnisotropic3D the
! reference value below is this solver's own answer, and the test is a regression
! lock rather than an oracle. What makes it a genuine one is that the checked norm
! distinguishes the branch it is meant to cover: with "Neo-Hookean Material"
! removed and the linear isotropic law used on the identical problem, stress_zz
! reads 4.324396577452E+001 against the 4.087361900855E+001 below, and stress_xz
! 1.065528154971E+001 against 9.719752715447E+000. So the value moves by 5.5% if
! this branch stops being taken -- four orders of magnitude outside the tolerance
! -- which is what a coverage test has to be able to say. It does not isolate the
! pressure term from the rest of the neo-Hookean response, and does not claim to.
!
! Displacement is prescribed on both ends and is large enough that the
! geometrically nonlinear terms matter; the linear system is direct so the result
! is reproducible to the last bit, which was verified across a rebuild.

Header
  Mesh DB "." "cube"
End

Simulation
  Max Output Level = 5
  Coordinate System = Cartesian
  Simulation Type = Steady State
  Steady State Max Iterations = 1
  Output Intervals = 0
End

Body 1
  Equation = 1
  Material = 1
End

Material 1
  Density = 1.0
  Youngs Modulus = 1.0e3
  Poisson Ratio = 0.3
End

Equation 1
  Active Solvers(2) = 1 2
End

Solver 1
  Equation = "Elasticity"
  Procedure = "ElasticSolve" "ElasticSolver"
  Variable = -dofs 3 Displacement

  Neo-Hookean Material = True

  Calculate Stresses = Logical True
  Calculate Strains = Logical True
  Displace Mesh = Logical False

  Linear System Solver = Direct
  Linear System Direct Method = UMFPack

  Nonlinear System Max Iterations = 30
  Nonlinear System Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-11
  Steady State Convergence Tolerance = 1.0e-9
End

Solver 2
  Equation = "SaveScalars"
  Procedure = "SaveData" "SaveScalars"
  Exec Solver = After Simulation
  Show Norm Index = 1
  Variable 1 = String "Stress_zz"
  Operator 1 = String "max abs"
  Variable 2 = String "Stress_xz"
  Operator 2 = String "max abs"
End

Boundary Condition 1
  Target Boundaries(1) = 5
  Displacement 1 = Real 0.0
  Displacement 2 = Real 0.0
  Displacement 3 = Real 0.0
End

Boundary Condition 2
  Target Boundaries(1) = 6
  Displacement 1 = Real 2.0e-2
  Displacement 2 = Real 1.0e-2
  Displacement 3 = Real 0.5e-2
End

Solver 2 :: Reference Norm = Real 4.087361900855E+001
Solver 2 :: Reference Norm Tolerance = Real 1.0e-5
RUN
